      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum for sertraline, which is 200 mg/day. Nothing in the information you gave me (normal renal and hepatic function, 70 kg, no allergies) would justify a dose that high. At that level the risks include serotonin syndrome, QT prolongation, seizures, and GI or bleeding complications.\n\nPlease check which of these applies:\n\n1. **Typo or unit error.** You may have meant 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily. Typical dosing is 50\u2013200 mg/day. For depression, it usually starts at 50 mg and is titrated up. For OCD or PTSD, it can start at 25\u201350 mg.\n2. **Deliberate supratherapeutic dose.** If this is intentional, for example a specialist-directed regimen, tell me and add a rationale. I can enter it with a note such as \"Dose exceeds labeled max. Confirmed by attending. Rationale: ___.\" Pharmacy will probably want to verify it too.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm 600 mg is intended, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
